<title>USA: FSA qualifies five muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies five muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Burr Ridge, Ill., $6 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Hibbing, Minn., $1.94 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Wayzata Independent School District No 284, Minn., $24.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Glendale School District, Pa., $3 million GOs, under MBIA's alternate bid program.</p>
<p>--Sunnyvale, Texas, $2.2 million certificates of participation.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
